      "line": 113,
      "body": "The report documents a delta policy but never records the resolved `base_sha` used to build `baselineInventory`. On fallback/manual/initial-push runs, consumers cannot reconstruct which commit was compared, so the baseline is not reproducible. Pass the resolved SHA into this Python block and include it in both vulnerability report payloads."
    },
    {
      "id": 4150069589,
      "path": "demo/scripts/ci/write-build-metadata.sh",
      "line": 13,
      "body": "These direct Maven goals use unversioned plugin prefixes. They do not execute the `validate`-bound Enforcer rule, so Maven may resolve different help/dependency plugin versions over time and change the supposedly reproducible reports. Invoke fully qualified, explicitly versioned plugin coordinates here."
    },
    {
      "id": 4150069621,
      "path": "demo/scripts/ci/run-negative-controls.sh",
      "line": 52,
      "body": "The required Enforcer artifact contains only the expected keyword, not the actual Enforcer output that matched it. This prevents reviewers from checking whether each failure was actionable; append the captured Maven log (or a bounded diagnostic excerpt) to the artifact after each successful control.\n\nThis issue also appears on line 64 of the same file."
    }
  ]
}

